The fix is correctly applied. Here's a summary:

## Bug Analysis

**Root Cause:** The `loadAlgolia()` method in `StoriesFragment.java` was missing filter logic for `filterWords` and `filterDomains`. 

**Why it happened:** The app uses two different code paths for loading stories:
1. **`loadStory()`** — used for normal HN API views (Ask, Show, Jobs). This method checks `filterWords` and `filterDomains` after loading each story.
2. **`loadAlgolia()`** — used for Algolia-backed views (Top 24h, Top 48h, Top 7d). This method was missing the filter checks entirely, only filtering out already-clicked stories.

When the user set "brain" as a filter word, stories with "brain" in the title were correctly filtered in normal views (via `loadStory()`), but not in Top 24/48 views (via `loadAlgolia()`).

## Fix Applied

Added filtering logic to `loadAlgolia()` in `StoriesFragment.java` (lines 742-765):

```java
// Filter by filter words and filter domains
ArrayList<String> words = Utils.getFilterWords(getContext());
ArrayList<String> domains = Utils.getFilterDomains(getContext());
Iterator<Story> filterIterator = stories.iterator();
while (filterIterator.hasNext()) {
    Story story = filterIterator.next();
    boolean shouldFilter = false;
    for (String phrase : words) {
        if (story.title.toLowerCase().contains(phrase.toLowerCase())) {
            shouldFilter = true;
            break;
        }
    }
    if (!shouldFilter && story.url != null) {
        for (String phrase : domains) {
            if (story.url.toLowerCase().contains(phrase.toLowerCase())) {
                shouldFilter = true;
                break;
            }
        }
    }
    if (shouldFilter) {
        filterIterator.remove();
    }
}
```

This mirrors the exact same filtering logic already present in `loadStory()`, ensuring consistency across all views. The filtering is case-insensitive and applies to both story titles (word filters) and story URLs (domain filters).

